{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393162-back-to-the-drawing-writing-table-catalog-mannikins","id":1393162,"title":"Back to the drawing / writing table: Catalog: Mannikins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-31T11:43:22-07:00","id":1393162,"title":"Back to the drawing / writing table: Catalog: Mannikins","content":"When the world was young and dinosaurs walked the Earth, and I was young and innocent, back in the 90s, I was a member of a community called Shadownessence. There I wrote, then discarded when Banality fell on my bones, several projects. Now, C20 has made me dream again of Arcadia and my lost youth, so I have reopened my old folders...<br /> <br /> Project at hand: Catalog: Mannikins<br /> <br /> I wonder if this would interesting enough to compile, clean and rewrite it, and offer it in the Storyteller's Vault...<br /> <br /> So, without further ado, I'm going to show you what I wrote back in the days:<br /> <br /> Catalog: Mannikins (Sample)<br /> (This was intended to lure... I mean, attract, people to the Project)<br /> <br /> **Beginning: Sample text: &quot;Catalog: Mannikins&quot;**<br /> <br /> What is Catalog: Mannikins?<br /> <br /> Welcome to Catalog: Mannikins, a resource text on the Phylum which bridges the gap between Inanimae and Kithain, between inanimate and animate: the mannikins.<br /> <br /> This book is organized as a fashion store, with several floors where you can wander around, going back and forth, looking around, selecting some goods and discarding others.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> <b>\u201cBasement: Johnny went shopping\u201d</b>: A short story about two Wilders that decide to stay in a department store after the closing time, \u201cjust to take a look around\u201d.<br /> <b>\u201c1<sup>st</sup> floor: Welcome to our store\u201d</b>: What you are reading now. Includes a short lexicon of terms used only by the mannikins.<br /> <b>\u201c2<sup>nd</sup> floor: Ancient history, modern ways\u201d</b>: In this chapter, we are told the story of the mannikins, and the phylum\u2019s point of view about some important milestones of fey history.<br /> <b>\u201c3<sup>rd</sup> floor: Fashionable &amp; D\u00e9mod\u00e9\u201d</b>: This chapter is devoted to the mannikins\u2019 \u201clifestyles\u201d. We are allowed to look at their tastes, preferences, and relationships with other kiths and supernatural creatures (in the cases they deign to think about them). The mannikins\u2019 fascination with the Heart\u2019s Riddle is also addressed here.<br /> <b>\u201c4<sup>th</sup> floor: Capecia, the Clockwork City\u201d</b>: A short tourist-guide to Capecia, the Clockwork City.<br /> <b>\u201c5<sup>th</sup> floor: The Unblinking People\u201d</b>: This chapter is the one full of game-info. Some adjusted rules, some revised/new abilities, a new Art, and some mannikin-only Merits and Flaws. Also, my table-top version of the mannikin Birthrights and Frailties that appear in the Shining Host Player\u2019s Guide.<br /> <b>\u201c6<sup>th</sup> floor: The Shape of People to Come\u201d</b>: Three pre-built mannikins, ready to be used as NPCs or PCs in any C: tD chronicle.<br /> <b>Attic: Crafters &amp; Bargains.</b><br /> Renowned mannikins, both famous and infamous.<br /> <br /> <b>Lexicon</b>:<br /> <b>Alberti:</b> Nickname for Craft mannikins of the Automata Style.<br /> <b>Automata:</b> A Style whose members posses Anchors with mobile, internal mechanical (or electronic) components. Automata mannikins are split between the advocates of Craft and those of Factory.<br /> <b>Bot</b>: Nickname for members of the \u010capek Salon (slightly derogative if not used by themselves!).<br /> <b>Capecia:</b> The most successful colony of the Empire of Dolls, the one that grew from being a stray outpost to become one of the Heart\u2019s Realms of the Deep Dreaming. Also called, \u201cThe City Untethered by Gravity Even\u201d, Capecia is not \u201cArcadia for the Inanimae\u201d, as some have said; as the mannikins have no desire to show outsiders the way to their true homeland, Capecia serves as the \u201cunofficial\u201d capital city of the Empire of Dolls; it is kind of simultaneously Vienna and Paris during the Second World War.<br /> <b>Ceremonial:</b> A gentle, but proud, Style whose members posses Anchors that represent religious figures or beings, including sepulchral statuary.<br /> <b>Copellian:</b> A member of the Copelli Salon.<br /> <b>Craft:</b> Philosophical impulse that serves as a common theoretical foundation for all Salons that advocate the methodical, careful construction of individualized Husks. The most important Craft Salon is the Copelli Salon.<br /> <b>Empire of Dolls</b>: Both the mannikins as a species, and their fabled homeland in the Dreaming. All mannikins are citizens of the Empire of Dolls, but not all citizens of the Empire of Dolls are mannikins.<br /> <b>Factory:</b> Philosophical impulse, opposed to the Craft, that underlines the party lines of all Salons that prefer mass-produced, orthodox, impersonal Husks. Hard-core Factory thinkers founded the \u010capek Salon.<br /> <b>Fashion:</b> the most common surviving Style and the \u201cdefault\u201d one for most mannikins. Members of the Fashion Style are bound to commercial or professional Anchors (i.e. Fashion mannequins)<br /> <b>Free-thought:</b> Philosophical impulse, opposed to both Craft and Factory, that advocates the personal individuality of each mannikin, unrestricted by the construction of the Husk. Rotwang is the main Free-thought Salon.<br /> <b>Jouet:</b> Besides Fashion, the most common surviving Style. Jouet mannikins are those whose Anchors are toys, dolls, teddy bears and the like.<br /> <b>Mannikins:</b> The most numerous of the phyla of the Empire of Dolls (and their rulers), and the only one remaining on Earth. Mannikins are bound to their Anchors, like all other Earth-dwelling Inanimae.<br /> <b>Manzolini:</b> A highly regarded, but uncommon Style, the members of which are bound to anatomical and medical models, specially those sculpted in wax during the 16th and 17th centuries.<br /> <b>Mechs (also Mechroids):</b> Nickname for Factory mannikins of the Automata style.<br /> <b>Natural:</b> A very uncommon Style, the members of which are bound to Gladeling Anchors (i.e. a stone sculpted in the human shape by the waves). There are very few Naturals on Earth.<br /> <b>Naturals:</b> Nickname for mannikins of the Natural style. Also, any Gladeling Inanimae.<br /> <b>Phidian: </b>A common, politically conservative Style, the members of which are bound to Anchors sculpted or forged in stone, metal or very rarely, wood.<br /> <b>Salons:</b> Schools of thought and philosophical and political impulses, similar to those held by the Kithain. Many \u201cSalons\u201d are born in Capecia, and then exported to Earth by visitors and travelers from that Realm; most are short-lived, but some others had existed for a long, long time. The most important Salons are \u010capek, Copelli, and Rotwang. Certain Styles are predominant in certain Salons (i.e. most Statues are Copellians), and Naturals tend to ignore them completely.<br /> <b>Sepulchrals (also Supplicants): </b>Nickname for mannikins of the Ceremonial style.<br /> <b>Statues (also Phidians, Golems):</b> Nickname for mannikins of the Phidian style.<br /> <b>Styles</b>: Non-hierarchical \u201ccastes\u201d of mannikin society, based on the Anchor each Mannikin is bound to. Styles are only relevant to the mannikins themselves, and to other Earth-bound Inanimae. Chimerical citizens of the Empire of Dolls (those that don\u2019t posses an Anchor) are unable or unwilling to understand the complexities of politics between different Styles. Of the many Styles that existed once on Earth, most of them have disappeared or become extinct, and only seven remain in significant numbers: Automata, Ceremonial, Fashion, Jouet, Natural, Manzolini and Phidian.<br /> <b>Top Models (also Fashion Victims):</b> Nickname for mannikins of the Fashion style.<br /> <b>Toys (also Game Partners):</b> Nickname for mannikins of the Jouet Style.<br /> <b>Unblinking People</b>: The mannikins. Blinking does not come naturally to the mannikins, and they must learn to blink to be able to pass off as human beings.<br /> <b>Wax Corpses (also Waxworks):</b> Nickname for mannikins of the Manzolini style.<br /> <br /> **Ending: Sample text: &quot;Catalog: Mannikins&quot;**<br /> <br /> <b>Sources and Bibliography:</b><br /> Many sources have influenced the text you are now reading.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Books:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Dreams and Nightmares.</b></li> <li><b>Inanimae: the Secret Way.</b></li> </ol></li> <li><b>Web Sites:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>\u201cLa Specola\u201d World-famous Italian collection of medical models sculpted in wax. (A must for Manzolini players!)</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><a href=\"http://www.specola.unifi.it/cere\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.specola.unifi.it/cere</a></b></li> </ol></li> <li><b>Fashion Windows: Mannequins. (Very interesting!)</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><a href=\"http://www.fashionwindows.com/mannequins\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fashionwindows.com/mannequins</a></b></li> </ol></li> </ol></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"}